          <Pad Id="HK5xczVOP6DOHXEQVThNOI" Bounds="636,543,462,115" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="There are different ways to create a preset. Let's take a snapshot of public channels capturing the current values of those channels. Providing a 'Name' for the preset we can store it to disk. Presets are saved as individual files in a folder called \presets next to your main .vl document. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The 'Name' of the preset can then be used to recall it.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="RzUIkifO9QuOcaZ9iwEq6V" Bounds="146,955,393,64" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="To recall a preset, click `Apply`. Don't forget to change the input value of the public channel (see 2.) beforehand to see the effect. Its output value will jump to the one saved in the preset.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
